      "reviewed": true,
      "translation": "The Blessed Lord said: They speak of the imperishable aśvattha tree as having its root above and its branches below, with the Vedas as its leaves; one who knows that tree knows the Veda. Śrīdhara identifies the upper root with the Supreme Person, the lower branches with Brahmā and other conditioned forms, and the leaves with the Vedas that sustain worldly life through prescribed action and its fruits.",
