      "reviewed": true,
      "translation": "Its branches spread below and above, nourished by the guṇas, with the objects of the senses as their tender shoots; its roots spread downward and upward, bound to action in the human world. Śrīdhara explains the lower roots as the latent desires for particular experiences, which lead people into corresponding actions.",
